319 |         :rtype: ``None`` or ``datetime`` or ```time_delta`` or ``int``
320 | 
321 |         Must return one of:
322 | 
323 |         :``None``:
324 |             This means the placeholder and the page will not even
325 |             consider this plugin when calculating the page expiration;
326 | 
327 |         :``datetime``:
328 |             A specific date and time (timezone-aware) in the future
329 |             when this plugin's content expires;
330 | 
331 |             .. important:: The returned ``datetime`` must be timezone-aware
332 |                            or the plugin will be ignored (with a warning)
333 |                            during expiration calculations.
334 | 
335 | 
336 |         :``datetime.timedelta``:
337 |             A timedelta instance indicating how long, relative to
338 |             the response timestamp that the content can be cached;
339 | 
340 |         :``int``:
341 |             An integer number of seconds that this plugin's content can be cached.
342 | 
343 |         There are constants are defined in ``cms.constants`` that may be
344 |         useful: :const:`~cms.constants.EXPIRE_NOW` and :data:`~cms.constants.MAX_EXPIRATION_TTL`.
345 | 
346 |         An integer value of 0 (zero) or :const:`~cms.constants.EXPIRE_NOW` effectively means "do not
347 |         cache". Negative values will be treated as `EXPIRE_NOW`. Values exceeding the value
348 |         `~cms.constants.MAX_EXPIRATION_TTL` will be set to that value.
349 | 
350 |         Negative `timedelta` values or those greater than `MAX_EXPIRATION_TTL`
351 |         will also be ranged in the same manner.
352 | 
353 |         Similarly, `datetime` values earlier than now will be treated as
354 |         `EXPIRE_NOW`. Values greater than `MAX_EXPIRATION_TTL` seconds in the
